# The index of a Structure (the book, structure-index): `S[i]` reads what slot i holds -- an untyped reference to the
# cell of an int field, to the pointer of a field without a value, to a nested Structure --, `S[i] := p` gives the slot
# another address after the field's admission, `length(S)` is the number of the fields.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call main().
